# lau-scheduler

> Tick-based task scheduling for game loops. Priority queues, recurring tasks, cancellations — everything a game loop needs, nothing it doesn't.

## What This Does

The heartbeat of the **Lau (Layered Agent-UI)** game loop. Every game tick, the scheduler decides what runs and when. Tasks have priorities (critical, high, normal, low, idle), can be one-shot or recurring, and can be cancelled mid-flight.

Built for deterministic game loops: same tick count + same task graph = same execution order. Every time.

## Quick Start

```rust
use lau_scheduler::{Scheduler, TaskPriority};

let mut sched = Scheduler::new();

// Schedule one-shot task
sched.schedule_once("load-biome", TaskPriority::Critical, || {
    println!("Loading biome...");
});

// Schedule recurring task every 60 ticks (once per second at 60fps)
let id = sched.schedule_recurring("update-physics", TaskPriority::High, 1, || {
    // Physics step
});

// Schedule delayed task
sched.schedule_delayed("spawn-npc", TaskPriority::Normal, 300, || {
    // Spawn after 5 seconds (300 ticks at 60fps)
});

// Game loop
loop {
    sched.tick(); // Runs all due tasks for this tick
}
```

## API Reference

### TaskPriority

| Variant | Use For |
|---------|---------|
| `Critical` | Game state saves, network sync |
| `High` | Physics, collision, input |
| `Normal` | AI, rendering, audio |
| `Low` | Particle effects, decorations |
| `Idle` | Background loading, analytics |

### Scheduler

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `Scheduler::new()` | Create scheduler |
| `sched.schedule_once(id, priority, task)` | One-shot task |
| `sched.schedule_recurring(id, priority, every_n, task)` | Repeating task |
| `sched.schedule_delayed(id, priority, delay, task)` | Delayed one-shot |
| `sched.cancel(id)` | Cancel a task |
| `sched.tick()` | Run all due tasks |
| `sched.pending_count()` | Tasks waiting |
| `sched.clear()` | Remove all |

